sponse and resolution. Workplace method: Set boundaries, observe reality, map the as-is flow, expose pain points, design to-be options and validate with participants. Example: Use Flowcharts, swimlanes and BPMN basics and retain evidence of the result. Quality and interview check: Verify the outcome, explain trade-offs and avoid: Drawing the assumed process without exceptions, owners or stakeholder validation. Example: When is a swimlane diagram particularly useful?","key_terms":[{"term":"Process Mapping","definition":"A practical capability used in process mapping work.","example":"Map student support from request submission through triage, response and resolution."},{"term":"BPMN","definition":"A practical capability used in process mapping work.","example":"Map student support from request submission through triage, response and resolution."}]},"principles":{"rules":[{"rule_number":1,"title":"Principle","explanation":"A process model shows actors, events, activities, decisions, handoffs, data and exceptions in the current or future state.","why_it_works":"Example: Map student support from request submission through triage, response and resolution.","exception":null},{"rule_number":2,"title":"Workplace method","explanation":"Set boundaries, observe reality, map the as-is flow, expose pain points, design to-be options and validate with participants.","why_it_works":"Example: Use Flowcharts, swimlanes and BPMN basics and retain evidence of the result.","exception":null},{"rule_number":3,"title":"Quality and interview check","explanation":"Verify the outcome, explain trade-offs and avoid: Drawing the assumed process without exceptions, owners or stakeholder validation.","why_it_works":"Example: When is a swimlane diagram particularly useful?","exception":null}],"important_distinctions":[]},"application_method":{"method_title":"Learn, configure, validate","method_overview":"Connect the idea to a practical workflow, then validate the outcome.","steps":[{"step_number":1,"title":"Understand","instruction":"Identify the process goal, actors, inputs and expected outcome.","reason":"A clear process prevents incorrect work.","student_check":"Can you explain the goal in one sentence?"},{"step_number":2,"title":"Apply","instruction":"Practise this workflow: Set boundaries, observe reality, map the as-is flow, expose pain points, design to-be options and validate with participants.","reason":"Hands-on execution turns knowledge into a reusable skill.","student_check":"Did you complete every required part?"},{"step_number":3,"title":"Validate","instruction":"Test the result, review the evidence and correct any gap.","reason":"Validation makes the work reliable and interview-ready.","student_check":"Does the result satisfy the stated outcome?"}],"use_when":"Use this workflow for apply work.","do_not_use_when":"Do not expose confidential information or skip verification.","faster_method":"Avoid this common mistake: Drawing the assumed process without exceptions, owners or stakeholder validation."},"worked_examples":[{"example_number":1,"title":"Guided practice","difficulty":"Foundation to applied","question_or_scenario":"Practise this workflow: Set boundaries, observe reality, map the as-is flow, expose pain points, design to-be options and validate with participants.","given_information":["Process Mapping","BPMN"],"reasoning_steps":[{"step_number":1,"explanation":"Review the apply requirements and define the expected result."},{"step_number":2,"explanation":"Map student support from request submission through triage, response and resolution."},{"step_number":3,"explanation":"Validate the outcome. Avoid this common mistake: Drawing the assumed process without exceptions, owners or stakeholder validation."}],"final_answer":"Set boundaries, observe reality, map the as-is flow, expose pain points, design to-be options and validate with participants.","why_the_answer_is_correct":"The result follows the defined process, covers the required element