e method: Split by workflow or rule, write user-value context, add Given-When-Then criteria, refine dependencies and prioritise. Example: Use Jira backlog and story mapping and retain evidence of the result. Quality and interview check: Verify the outcome, explain trade-offs and avoid: Using the story format for large projects or writing acceptance criteria as design instructions only. Example: What makes a story ready for development?","key_terms":[{"term":"User Stories","definition":"A practical capability used in user stories and agile work.","example":"As a student, I can submit a support request and receive a reference so I can track that help was requested."},{"term":"Agile","definition":"A practical capability used in user stories and agile work.","example":"As a student, I can submit a support request and receive a reference so I can track that help was requested."},{"term":"Jira","definition":"A practical capability used in user stories and agile work.","example":"As a student, I can submit a support request and receive a reference so I can track that help was requested."}]},"principles":{"rules":[{"rule_number":1,"title":"Principle","explanation":"A user story expresses a small valuable capability, while acceptance criteria make expected behaviour testable.","why_it_works":"Example: As a student, I can submit a support request and receive a reference so I can track that help was requested.","exception":null},{"rule_number":2,"title":"Workplace method","explanation":"Split by workflow or rule, write user-value context, add Given-When-Then criteria, refine dependencies and prioritise.","why_it_works":"Example: Use Jira backlog and story mapping and retain evidence of the result.","exception":null},{"rule_number":3,"title":"Quality and interview check","explanation":"Verify the outcome, explain trade-offs and avoid: Using the story format for large projects or writing acceptance criteria as design instructions only.","why_it_works":"Example: What makes a story ready for development?","exception":null}],"important_distinctions":[]},"application_method":{"method_title":"Learn, configure, validate","method_overview":"Connect the idea to a practical workflow, then validate the outcome.","steps":[{"step_number":1,"title":"Understand","instruction":"Identify the process goal, actors, inputs and expected outcome.","reason":"A clear process prevents incorrect work.","student_check":"Can you explain the goal in one sentence?"},{"step_number":2,"title":"Apply","instruction":"Practise this workflow: Split by workflow or rule, write user-value context, add Given-When-Then criteria, refine dependencies and prioritise.","reason":"Hands-on execution turns knowledge into a reusable skill.","student_check":"Did you complete every required part?"},{"step_number":3,"title":"Validate","instruction":"Test the result, review the evidence and correct any gap.","reason":"Validation makes the work reliable and interview-ready.","student_check":"Does the result satisfy the stated outcome?"}],"use_when":"Use this workflow for understand work.","do_not_use_when":"Do not expose confidential information or skip verification.","faster_method":"Avoid this common mistake: Using the story format for large projects or writing acceptance criteria as design instructions only."},"worked_examples":[{"example_number":1,"title":"Guided practice","difficulty":"Foundation to applied","question_or_scenario":"Practise this workflow: Split by workflow or rule, write user-value context, add Given-When-Then criteria, refine dependencies and prioritise.","given_information":["User Stories","Agile","Jira"],"reasoning_steps":[{"step_number":1,"explanation":"Review the understand requirements and define the expected result."},{"step_number":2,"explanation":"As a student, I can submit a support request and receive a reference so I can track that help was requested."},{"step_number":3,"explanation":"Validate the outcome. Avoid this common mistake: Using the story format for large projects or writing acceptance criteria as design instructions only."}],"final_answer":"Split by workflow or rule, write user-value context, add Given-When-Then criteria, refine dependencies and prioritise.","why_the_answer_is_correct":"The result follows the defined process, covers the required elements and includes a validation step.","learning_takeaway":"Avoid this common mistake: Using the story format for large projects or writing acceptance criteria as design instructions only."}],"usage_comparisons":[],"common_mistakes":[{"mistake_number":1,"title":"Acting before understanding","incorrect_approach":"Starting immediately without confirming scope, inputs and success criteria.","why_students_make_it":"Speed can feel more important than process discipline.","why_it_is_wrong":"An incomplete process creates unreliable results and avoidable rework.","correction":"Define the outcome, complete the workflow, and validate it once.","prevention_tip":"Avoid this common mistake: Using the story format for large projects or writing acceptance criteria as design instructions only."}],"memory_support":{"memory_aid":"Avoid this common mistake: Using the story format for large projects or writing acceptance criteria as design instructions only.","mental_model":"Concept → Practice → Proof","quick_recall_note":"Understand → Apply → Validate"},"placement_support":{"question_identification_signals":["Understand","User Stories and Agile: Core Concepts","User Stories","Agile"],"time_management_tip":"Avoid this common mistake: Using the story format for large projects or writing acceptance criteria as design instructions only.","exam_traps":["Skipping context","Ignoring edge cases or validation"],"interview_relevance":"Use the completed activity and its validation evidence to explain your approach in interviews."},"checkpoint_questions":[{"question_number":1,"type":"application","question":"In your own words, what problem does user stories and agile solve?","answer":"A user story expresses a small valuable capability, while acceptance criteria make expected behaviour testable.","explanation":"A strong answer states the business or user problem before naming a tool.","skill_tested":"User Stories and Agile: Core Concepts","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"},{"question_number":2,"type":"reasoning","question":"How would you apply this capability in the following workplace situation: As a student, I can submit a support request and receive a reference so I can track that help was requested.","answer":"Split by workflow or rule, write user-value context, add Given-When-Then criteria, refine dependencies and prioritise.","explanation":"The response should describe a controlled, verifiable workflow rather than only a feature.","skill_tested":"User Stories and Agile: Core Concepts","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"},{"question_number":3,"type":"application","question":"What makes a story ready for development?","answer":"Use A user story expresses a small valuable capability, while acceptance criteria make expected behaviour testable. Then describe the workflow: Split by workflow or rule, write user-value context, add Given-When-Then criteria, refine dependencies and prioritise.","explanation":"Interview answers should connect principle, action, validation and outcome.","skill_tested":"User Stories and Agile: Core Concepts","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"}],"remediation":{"likely_confusion":"The concept may feel abstract before it is connected to a practical workflow.","simplified_explanation":"A user story expresses a small valuable capability, while acceptance criteria make expected behaviour testable.","simple_example":"As a student, I can submit a support request and receive a reference so I can track that help was requested.","prerequisite_to_review":"Understand","next_recommended_step":"Practise this workflow: Split by workflow or rule, write user-value context, add Given-When-Then criteria, refine dependencies and prioritise."},"