ge, monitoring and cost safeguards.","exception":null},{"rule_number":2,"title":"Build and validate","explanation":"Complete the workflow using controlled data, appropriate tools and recorded checks.","why_it_works":"Example: Retain source, working files and a short validation log.","exception":null},{"rule_number":3,"title":"Present","explanation":"Communicate the outcome, evidence, trade-offs and next action concisely.","why_it_works":"Example: Use a problem-action-result-reflection interview narrative.","exception":null}],"important_distinctions":[]},"application_method":{"method_title":"Learn, configure, validate","method_overview":"Connect the idea to a practical workflow, then validate the outcome.","steps":[{"step_number":1,"title":"Understand","instruction":"Identify the process goal, actors, inputs and expected outcome.","reason":"A clear process prevents incorrect work.","student_check":"Can you explain the goal in one sentence?"},{"step_number":2,"title":"Apply","instruction":"Create and explain a small AWS architecture with identity controls, networking, compute, storage, monitoring and cost safeguards.","reason":"Hands-on execution turns knowledge into a reusable skill.","student_check":"Did you complete every required part?"},{"step_number":3,"title":"Validate","instruction":"Test the result, review the evidence and correct any gap.","reason":"Validation makes the work reliable and interview-ready.","student_check":"Does the result satisfy the stated outcome?"}],"use_when":"Use this workflow for final assessment work.","do_not_use_when":"Do not expose confidential information or skip verification.","faster_method":"Demonstrate judgement and verification; do not submit disconnected screenshots or unsupported claims."},"worked_examples":[{"example_number":1,"title":"Guided practice","difficulty":"Applied entry-level","question_or_scenario":"Create and explain a small AWS architecture with identity controls, networking, compute, storage, monitoring and cost safeguards.","given_information":["AWS","Cloud Computing","IAM","Networking","EC2","S3","Cloud Security"],"reasoning_steps":[{"step_number":1,"explanation":"Review the final assessment requirements and define the expected result."},{"step_number":2,"explanation":"Present the final deliverable as if handing it to a manager or interviewer. Include the problem, method, evidence, result and limitation."},{"step_number":3,"explanation":"Validate the outcome. Demonstrate judgement and verification; do not submit disconnected screenshots or unsupported claims."}],"final_answer":"A complete submission achieves this outcome: Create and explain a small AWS architecture with identity controls, networking, compute, storage, monitoring and cost safeguards.","why_the_answer_is_correct":"The result follows the defined process, covers the required elements and includes a validation step.","learning_takeaway":"Demonstrate judgement and verification; do not submit disconnected screenshots or unsupported claims."}],"usage_comparisons":[],"common_mistakes":[{"mistake_number":1,"title":"Acting before understanding","incorrect_approach":"Starting immediately without confirming scope, inputs and success criteria.","why_students_make_it":"Speed can feel more important than process discipline.","why_it_is_wrong":"An incomplete process creates unreliable results and avoidable rework.","correction":"Define the outcome, complete the workflow, and validate it once.","prevention_tip":"Demonstrate judgement and verification; do not submit disconnected screenshots or unsupported claims."}],"memory_support":{"memory_aid":"Demonstrate judgement and verification; do not submit disconnected screenshots or unsupported claims.","mental_model":"Concept → Practice → Proof","quick_recall_note":"Understand → Apply → Validate"},"placement_support":{"question_identification_signals":["Final assessment","AWS & Cloud Fundamentals: Final Assessment & Portfolio Review","AWS","Cloud Computing"],"time_management_tip":"Demonstrate judgement and verification; do not submit disconnected screenshots or unsupported claims.","exam_traps":["Skipping context","Ignoring edge cases or validation"],"interview_relevance":"Use the completed activity and its validation evidence to explain your approach in interviews."},"checkpoint_questions":[{"question_number":1,"type":"application","question":"What problem and user does your capstone address?","answer":"State a specific user, decision and measurable outcome.","explanation":"A portfolio project needs a real purpose.","skill_tested":"AWS & Cloud Fundamentals: Final Assessment & Portfolio Review","difficulty":"Applied entry-level"},{"question_number":2,"type":"reasoning","question":"Which evidence proves the result is correct?","answer":"Provide reconciliation, tests or review evidence appropriate to the course.","explanation":"Visible validation builds trust.","skill_tested":"AWS & Cloud Fundamentals: Final Assessment & Portfolio Review","difficulty":"Applied entry-level"},{"question_number":3,"type":"application","question":"What was the most important trade-off?","answer":"Name the alternatives, constraint, decision and consequence.","explanation":"Trade-offs demonstrate judgement.","skill_tested":"AWS & Cloud Fundamentals: Final Assessment & Portfolio Review","difficulty":"Applied entry-level"},{"question_number":4,"type":"application","question":"What limitation remains?","answer":"State one honest boundary and how future work could address it.","explanation":"Professional communication does not overclaim.","skill_tested":"AWS & Cloud Fundamentals: Final Assessment & Portfolio Review","difficulty":"Applied entry-level"},{"question_number":5,"type":"application","question":"Explain your project in 90 seconds.","answer":"Use problem, action, validated result and reflection.","explanation":"This structure creates a concise interview story.","skill_tested":"AWS & Cloud Fundamentals: Final Assessment & Portfolio Review","difficulty":"App