evel work and is assessed through practical scenarios and interviews.","concept_explanation":"Principle: Qualification tests fit, need, impact, authority, process and timing while discovery uncovers the customer''s current reality. Example: A discovery call explores current student preparation, completion, reporting and procurement constraints. Workplace method: Prepare hypotheses, ask open and diagnostic questions, listen, summarise, quantify impact and agree next steps. Example: Use Discovery guide and qualification framework and retain evidence of the result. Quality and interview check: Verify the outcome, explain trade-offs and avoid: Interrogating prospects, leading them to desired answers or qualifying only on budget. Example: Which discovery questions reveal impact rather than surface preference?","key_terms":[{"term":"Lead Qualification","definition":"A practical capability used in qualification and discovery work.","example":"A discovery call explores current student preparation, completion, reporting and procurement constraints."},{"term":"Discovery","definition":"A practical capability used in qualification and discovery work.","example":"A discovery call explores current student preparation, completion, reporting and procurement constraints."}]},"principles":{"rules":[{"rule_number":1,"title":"Principle","explanation":"Qualification tests fit, need, impact, authority, process and timing while discovery uncovers the customer''s current reality.","why_it_works":"Example: A discovery call explores current student preparation, completion, reporting and procurement constraints.","exception":null},{"rule_number":2,"title":"Workplace method","explanation":"Prepare hypotheses, ask open and diagnostic questions, listen, summarise, quantify impact and agree next steps.","why_it_works":"Example: Use Discovery guide and qualification framework and retain evidence of the result.","exception":null},{"rule_number":3,"title":"Quality and interview check","explanation":"Verify the outcome, explain trade-offs and avoid: Interrogating prospects, leading them to desired answers or qualifying only on budget.","why_it_works":"Example: Which discovery questions reveal impact rather than surface preference?","exception":null}],"important_distinctions":[]},"application_method":{"method_title":"Learn, configure, validate","method_overview":"Connect the idea to a practical workflow, then validate the outcome.","steps":[{"step_number":1,"title":"Understand","instruction":"Identify the process goal, actors, inputs and expected outcome.","reason":"A clear process prevents incorrect work.","student_check":"Can you explain the goal in one sentence?"},{"step_number":2,"title":"Apply","instruction":"Complete this workplace lab: A discovery call explores current student preparation, completion, reporting and procurement constraints.","reason":"Hands-on execution turns knowledge into a reusable skill.","student_check":"Did you complete every required part?"},{"step_number":3,"title":"Validate","instruction":"Test the result, review the evidence and correct any gap.","reason":"Validation makes the work reliable and interview-ready.","student_check":"Does the result satisfy the stated outcome?"}],"use_when":"Use this workflow for assess work.","do_not_use_when":"Do not expose confidential information or skip verification.","faster_method":"Avoid this common mistake: Interrogating prospects, leading them to desired answers or qualifying only on budget."},"worked_examples":[{"example_number":1,"title":"Guided practice","difficulty":"Foundation to applied","question_or_scenario":"Complete this workplace lab: A discovery call explores current student preparation, completion, reporting and procurement constraints.","given_information":["Lead Qualification","Discovery"],"reasoning_steps":[{"step_number":1,"explanation":"Review the assess requirements and define the expected result."},{"step_number":2,"explanation":"A discovery call explores current student preparation, completion, reporting and procurement constraints."},{"step_number":3,"explanation":"Validate the outcome. Avoid this common mistake: Interrogating prospects, leading them to desired answers or qualifying only on budget."}],"final_answer":"A complete submission uses Discovery guide and qualification framework, follows the workflow, records validation evidence and explains one limitation.","why_the_answer_is_correct":"The result follows the defined process, covers the required elements and includes a validation step.","learning_takeaway":"Avoid this common mistake: Interrogating prospects, leading them to desired answers or qualifying only on budget."}],"usage_comparisons":[],"common_mistakes":[{"mistake_number":1,"title":"Acting before understanding","incorrect_approach":"Starting immediately without confirming scope, inputs and success criteria.","why_students_make_it":"Speed can feel more important than process discipline.","why_it_is_wrong":"An incomplete process creates unreliable results and avoidable rework.","correction":"Define the outcome, complete the workflow, and validate it once.","prevention_tip":"Avoid this common mistake: Interrogating prospects, leading them to desired answers or qualifying only on budget."}],"memory_support":{"memory_aid":"Avoid this common mistake: Interrogating prospects, leading them to desired answers or qualifying only on budget.","mental_model":"Concept → Practice → Proof","quick_recall_note":"Understand → Apply → Validate"},"placement_support":{"question_identification_signals":["Assess","Qualification and Discovery: Workplace Lab & Module Check","Lead Qualification","Discovery"],"time_management_tip":"Avoid this common mistake: Interrogating prospects, leading them to desired answers or qualifying only on budget.","exam_traps":["Skipping context","Ignoring edge cases or validation"],"interview_relevance":"Use the completed activity and its validation evidence to explain your approach in interviews."},"checkpoint_questions":[{"question_number":1,"type":"application","question":"In your own words, what problem does qualification and discovery solve?","answer":"Qualification tests fit, need, impact, authority, process and timing while discovery uncovers the customer''s current reality.","explanation":"A strong answer states the business or user problem before naming a tool.","skill_tested":"Qualification and Discovery: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"},{"question_number":2,"type":"reasoning","question":"How would you apply this capability in the following workplace situation: A discovery call explores current student preparation, completion, reporting and procurement constraints.","answer":"Prepare hypotheses, ask open and diagnostic questions, listen, summarise, quantify impact and agree next steps.","explanation":"The response should describe a controlled, verifiable workflow rather than only a feature.","skill_tested":"Qualification and Discovery: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"},{"question_number":3,"type":"application","question":"Which discovery questions reveal impact rather than surface preference?","answer":"Use Qualification tests fit, need, impact, authority, process and timing while discovery uncovers the customer''s current reality. Then describe the workflow: Prepare hypotheses, ask open and diagnostic questions, listen, summarise, quantify impact and agree next steps.","explanation":"Interview answers should connect principle, action, validation and outcome.","skill_tested":"Qualification and Discovery: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"},{"question_number":4,"type":"application","question":"Identify the main risk in this incorrect approach: Interrogating prospects, leading them to desired answers or qualifying only on budget.","answer":"The approach is unreliable because it breaks the controls implied by Qualification tests fit, need, impact, authority, process and timing while discovery uncovers the customer''s current reality.","explanation":"The correction should address cause and verification, not only appearance.","skill_tested":"Qualification and Discovery: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"},{"question_number":5,"type":"application","question":"Which tool or artefact would you use first, and what would you verify?","answer":"Use Discovery guide and qualification framework; verify that the result satisfies the stated decision, data and quality requirements.","explanation":"Tools support a method; they do not replace validation.","skill_tested":"Qualification and Discovery: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation to applied"}],"remediation":{"likely_confusion":"The concept may feel abstract before it is connected to a practical workflow.","simplified_explanation":"Apply Qualification tests fit, need, impact, authority, process and timing while discovery uncovers the customer''s current reality. Complete the scenario, produce evidence, explain the decision and correct the common failure: Interrogating prospects, leading them to desired answers or qualifying only on budget.","simple_example":"A discovery call explores current student preparation, completion, reporting and procurement constraints.","prerequisite_to_review":"Assess","next_recommended_step":"Complete this workplace lab: A discovery call explores current student preparation, completion, reporting and procurement constraints."},"revision_asset":{"summary":"Apply Qualification tests fit, need, impact, authority, process and timing while discovery uncovers the customer''s current reality. Complete the scenario, produce evidence, explain the decision and correct the common failure: Interrogating prospects, leading them to desired answers or qualifying only on budget.","key_points":["Lead Qualification","Discovery","Avoid this common mistake: Interrogating prospects, leading them to desired answers or qualifying only on budget."],"one_minute_revision":"Qualification and Discovery: Workplace Lab & Module Check: Apply Qualification tests fit, need, impact, authority, process and timing while discovery uncovers the customer''s current reality. Complete the scenario, produce evidence, explain the decision and correct the common failure: Interrogating prospects, leading them to desired answers or qualifying only on budget.","final_checklist":["I can explain the concept.","I can complete the activity.","I can validate and present the result."]},"quality_metadata":{"content_origin":"taksh_authored","review_status":"approved","copyright_review_status":"original","prompt_version":"deterministic-v2","generated_by":"taksh","sections_not_applicable":[]}}'::jsonb,1,now(),now(),now(),array['Lead Qualification','Discovery']::text[]
