 in entry-level work and is assessed through practical scenarios and interviews.","concept_explanation":"Principle: Office tools create more value when information flows predictably between data, documents, presentations and collaboration. Example: An Excel status table supplies charts for a PowerPoint review and actions for a Teams follow-up. Workplace method: Identify source data, create reusable outputs, link rather than duplicate where safe, refresh, validate and distribute. Example: Use Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook and Teams and retain evidence of the result. Quality and interview check: Verify the outcome, explain trade-offs and avoid: Copying numbers manually across files without recording source or refresh date. Example: How would you prevent inconsistent figures across a report and presentation?","key_terms":[{"term":"MS Office","definition":"A practical capability used in integrated office workflows work.","example":"An Excel status table supplies charts for a PowerPoint review and actions for a Teams follow-up."},{"term":"Automation","definition":"A practical capability used in integrated office workflows work.","example":"An Excel status table supplies charts for a PowerPoint review and actions for a Teams follow-up."},{"term":"Workplace Productivity","definition":"A practical capability used in integrated office workflows work.","example":"An Excel status table supplies charts for a PowerPoint review and actions for a Teams follow-up."}]},"principles":{"rules":[{"rule_number":1,"title":"Principle","explanation":"Office tools create more value when information flows predictably between data, documents, presentations and collaboration.","why_it_works":"Example: An Excel status table supplies charts for a PowerPoint review and actions for a Teams follow-up.","exception":null},{"rule_number":2,"title":"Workplace method","explanation":"Identify source data, create reusable outputs, link rather than duplicate where safe, refresh, validate and distribute.","why_it_works":"Example: Use Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook and Teams and retain evidence of the result.","exception":null},{"rule_number":3,"title":"Quality and interview check","explanation":"Verify the outcome, explain trade-offs and avoid: Copying numbers manually across files without recording source or refresh date.","why_it_works":"Example: How would you prevent inconsistent figures across a report and presentation?","exception":null}],"important_distinctions":[]},"application_method":{"method_title":"Learn, configure, validate","method_overview":"Connect the idea to a practical workflow, then validate the outcome.","steps":[{"step_number":1,"title":"Understand","instruction":"Identify the process goal, actors, inputs and expected outcome.","reason":"A clear process prevents incorrect work.","student_check":"Can you explain the goal in one sentence?"},{"step_number":2,"title":"Apply","instruction":"Complete this workplace lab: An Excel status table supplies charts for a PowerPoint review and actions for a Teams follow-up.","reason":"Hands-on execution turns knowledge into a reusable skill.","student_check":"Did you complete every required part?"},{"step_number":3,"title":"Validate","instruction":"Test the result, review the evidence and correct any gap.","reason":"Validation makes the work reliable and interview-ready.","student_check":"Does the result satisfy the stated outcome?"}],"use_when":"Use this workflow for assess work.","do_not_use_when":"Do not expose confidential information or skip verification.","faster_method":"Avoid this common mistake: Copying numbers manually across files without recording source or refresh date."},"worked_examples":[{"example_number":1,"title":"Guided practice","difficulty":"Foundation to applied","question_or_scenario":"Complete this workplace lab: An Excel status table supplies charts for a PowerPoint review and actions for a Teams follow-up.","given_information":["MS Office","Automation","Workplace Productivity"],"rea